  "description": "This course covers fundamental concepts and advanced topics in distributed systems, including communication protocols such as HTTP/REST, gRPC, and MQTT; consensus algorithms like Paxos and Raft; distributed data storage using technologies such as Cassandra, MongoDB, and HBase; fault tolerance mechanisms including replication, sharding, and consistency models; distributed transactions using two-phase commit and three-phase commit protocols; load balancing techniques such as round-robin and least connections; distributed file systems like HDFS and Ceph; distributed computing frameworks such as Apache Spark and MapReduce; and security considerations such as TLS, PKI, and authentication mechanisms. The course also explores cloud-native architectures, microservices, and serverless computing using platforms like Kubernetes, Docker, and AWS Lambda.",
